 "final_summary": "The bug was that non-positive values from environment variables were being directly used as config values without falling back to the default. The fix modifies the `_coerce` function in `tracker/config.py` to reject non-positive integers and fall back to the default value (20). This ensures that values like -5 from the environment are properly handled and do not override the default page size.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex 9d02783..ae2cb94 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ def _coerce(name, value):\n             number = int(str(value).strip())\n         except (TypeError, ValueError):\n             return None\n-        return number\n+        return number if number > 0 else DEFAULTS[name]\n     if value is None:\n         return None\n     text = str(value)\n",
